{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/628209-deadpool-as-an-unchained-cipher","id":628209,"title":"Deadpool As An Unchained + Cipher","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-15T22:15:40-07:00","id":628209,"title":"Deadpool As An Unchained + Cipher","content":"Since my write up of the Doctor as a Demon was well received, I figured that it would be fun to see if another one of my favorite characters works as a Demon: our very own Merc With The Mouth. Unfortunately, I am really unsure about which parts of his backstory need to be altered for the NWOD and how to alter them. On the other hand, you could portray him sort of like the Joker as seen in Dark Knight: there are no records or documents that might point towards his origin. However, he does care about the money and has standards for what missions he'll take. The emphasis would be put on unpredictability and delusions of grandeur, rather than a dark nihilism or cruelty. He can be an ally or an enemy as the plot requires.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Cunning<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Loudmouthed/Hedonistic<br /> <br /> <b>Incarnation:</b> Destroyer<br /> <b>Agenda:</b> None (Or Tempter)<br /> <b>Catalyst:</b> Unscheduled Demolition<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Wisecracking Lunatic Assassin<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 6, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2, Crafts (Firearm Maintenance) 3, Computer (Hide Footprints) 3, Medicine 3, Occult 2, Politics 1, Investigation (Marks) 3, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Drive 2, Firearms (Pistols) 5, Larceny 2, Stealth (Shadowing) 4, Survival 2, Weaponry (Swords) 5<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 1, Expression (Humor) 3, Intimidation (Batshit Crazy) 3, Persuasion 3, Socialize 0, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge (Fast Talking) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Vice-Ridden, Area Of Expertise (Firearm Maintenance, Hide Footprints), Tolerance for Biology, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Humor, Fast Talking, Batshit Crazy), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Firearms, Weaponry), Professional Training 5 (Hit Man: Stealth, Firearms, Weaponry), Ambidextrous, Gunslinger, Quick Draw (Pistols, Swords), Fighting Finesse (Swords), Heavy Weapons (Swords) 4, Martial Arts 3, Marksmanship 3, Parkour 4, Iron Stamina 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Fast Reflexes 3, Hardy 3, Quick Healer, Resources 5, Contacts X (Frequent Clients), Fixer, Anonymity 5, Living The Lie, Resonance Sensitive, Resonance Aware 3, Versatile Transformation, Terrible Form 4, Advance Form, Bolthole 11 (No Twilight 1, Arsenal 5, Trap Door 2, Easy Access 3)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Embeds</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Vocal:</b> Eavesdrop, Find The Leak, Voice Of The Machine, Vox<br /> <br /> <b>Instrumental:</b> Call Out, Check Backdrop, Data Retrieval, Data Wipe, Efficiency, Miles Away, Open Sesame, Right Tools Right Job, Tag And Release<br /> <br /> <b>Cacophony:</b> Breakdown, Bystander Effect, Cause And Effect, Cool Heads Prevail, Hush, Just Bruised, Knockout Punch, Merciless Gunman, On The Mend, Ripple, Special Someone<br /> <br /> <b>Mundane:</b> Deep Cover, Going Native, Identity Theft, In My Pocket, Like The Movies, Lost In The Crowd, Never Here, Quick Change, Without A Trace<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Exploits</b></span><br /> <br /> Behind The Curtain, Context Matters, Deep Pockets<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Demonic Form</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Modifications:</b> Armored Plates, Blade Hand, Resistors, Rivet Arm, Tough As Stone<br /> <br /> <b>Technologies:</b> Mirrored Skin, Laser Cutter, Shielded Compartment<br /> <br /> <b>Propulsions:</b> Long Limbs, Plasma Drive<br /> <br /> <b>Processes:</b> Body Modification, Eliminator Cannon, Wound Healing<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Primum:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Cipher</b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Play Along</b></span><br /> <br /> Deadpool actively tries to appear as removed from reality as possible, but that persona is a calculated one. This dismissal is often what brings down other people\u2019s guard while he sets his plans and shenanigans in motion.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Miles Away</i> and <i>Breakdown</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge - Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Deadpool appears to be even more dangerous than he is, and those present gain the Steadfast Condition and +2 to all rolls meant to oppose him for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. He may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Deadpool doesn\u2019t seem like a major threat as his past actions may indicate. He gains the Leveraged Condition for the purposes of convincing others to give up on opposing him right now.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Deadpool appears so insignificant and easy to predict that any rolls meant to fool people into overlooking him gain a +2 bonus.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Look At That Over There</b></span><br /> <br /> With prying eyes away from him, Deadpool can get away with a whole lot in very little time. He uses this opportunity to move the pieces further by avoiding the obvious.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Breakdown</i> and <i>Cause And Effect</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Stealth - Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Deadpool is firmly locked up in his own little world as he carries along. He is considered to roll only a chance die to acknowledge anyone calling his attention and/or inserting flaws into his plans. This may inflict a -3 to -5 penalty on the next Interlock.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. He may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Deadpool gains the Inspired Condition for all Physical and Mental actions related to setting up traps, schemes, false clues, pranks and the like. This Condition is applied to a number of rolls equal to his Primum/2 round up.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Apply the Condition to a number of rolls equal to his whole Primum. Said rolls also get 8 Again.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Did Not See That Coming</b></span><br /> <br /> Deadpool may have a pathological difficulty with telling reality apart from his delusions, but this instability is compensated with a level of ingenuity that makes his opponents regret underestimating him.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Cause And Effect</i> and <i>Ripple</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Expression - Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Deadpool suffers two Tilts that were meant for his opponents. These Tilts are chosen by the ST and must last for a minimum of one scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. He may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>Whatever it is that he planned or improvised, Deadpool can trigger a chain reaction with a statement. He may apply a number of Tilts equal to his Primum, which must be relevant to whatever mechanisms and distractions he set up previously. These Tilts can be customized to incapacitate supernatural or unusual targets that would normally have measures against them. He gains the Informed Condition regarding any course of action that his opponents might take to avoid or resolve the Tilts.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Deadpool triggers the events in such an over the top way that he feels invincible, and his opponents are dumbstruck. He regains all Willpower Points, and those who fail a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll penalized by his successes lose their turn.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-16-2015, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T00:09:08-07:00","id":628269,"title":"","content":"I'd totally say he's Tempter/Saboteur","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T16:24:58-07:00","id":629161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/628209-deadpool-as-an-unchained-cipher?p=628269#post628269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd totally say he's Tempter/Saboteur</div> </div> </div> </div> If I were to give him an Agenda, I would make him a Tempter only. He does love the many benefits of large sums of money. I don't think he'd be a Saboteur because destroying the God-Machine might cause world wide disaster, and the world is where he keeps all of his stuff. He might help Saboteurs here and there, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T20:58:12-07:00","id":630618,"title":"","content":"And for Deadpool, Loudmouthed is <u>totally</u> a virtue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}